Subject: [PATCH] AL-SAP: retain live Wi-Fi membership in topology responses

The AL-SAP proxy replaced the HLE's Device Information with a kernel-derived
inventory that has empty media-specific data. This erased the live backhaul
BSSID after reparenting. Periodic topology and capability reports then exposed
different parents although the radio stayed associated to the new AP.

Keep the AL database's identity and interface roster, merging only complete
Wi-Fi media data from a uniquely matching local HLE interface and AL MAC.
Preserve supplied opaque Wi-Fi 6/7 media bytes when serializing instead of
silently dropping them. Empty media information remains empty. No EasyMesh
agent/controller code or topology-selection policy changes are required.

Upstream-Status: Pending

